KZ3 patch 2077 (RSX pass 73): the VP start slot in the pipeline key; the shipped pipeline template loads by default.
the RE notes "Pass 73".
1. The walker keys a pipeline by the VP words, but ld_xlate decompiles with rsx_vp_set_branch_base(vp_start): a
   branching program's absolute targets become relative to its start slot, so the same words uploaded at two slots
   give two shaders under one key (the 8-chapter template merge saw 881 such clashes). rsx_vp_key_branch_base folds the
   start slot into the key for programs with a flow instruction (rsx_vp_has_flow, the decompiler's own leader scan);
   branch-free keys are unchanged, so pso_keys.bin and template records of branch-free programs stay valid. Stale
   records of branching programs fail the prewarm's key recompute ("key mismatch") and are never used.
2. LD_PSO_TEMPLATE unset: <exe dir>\pso-template.bin, else <exe dir>\..\pso-template.bin (the release keeps kz3.exe
   in build\ and the template in the install root) is prewarmed when it exists. LD_PSO_TEMPLATE=0 turns it off.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): both (branch-bits key from the rebase, then 2077's branch-base key).

